<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Feb 20.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Feb 20.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>Karavomarjds	28/01/97		  -	    Africa</p>
<p>Samjiang	    28/01/97		3,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>Delight	     30/01/97		5,700	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Jrace Luna	  30/01/97		4,500	  Japan</p>
<p>Saigon 2	    30/01/97		9,000	  Vietnam</p>
<p>Sunchon	     30/01/97		7,000	  Vietnam</p>
<p>Sangthai Radium   30/01/97		  -	    Singapore</p>
<p>Sangthai Eagle    30/01/97		  -	    Hong Kong</p>
<p>Pichit Navy	 30/01/97		  -	    Cambodia</p>
<p>Sangthai Ocean    03/02/97		  -	    Hong Kong</p>
<p>Bang Khuntien     04/02/97		5,700	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Sierra Madre	06/02/97		5,500	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Argus		 07/02/97		4,000	  Japan</p>
<p>Sangthai Ceramic  10/02/97		  -	    Singapore</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
